"""Editorial question designs for wedding culture, folk traditions, and folk theatre."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


WEDDING_CULTURE = """history_origins|Tracing One Wedding Custom|What can dated sources establish about a specific custom?|Name community and distinguish surviving evidence from absolute origin.
famous_examples|A Publicly Celebrated Wedding Rite|What does one well-known rite mean to current practitioners?|Compare participant accounts with outside portrayals.
hidden_stories|Work Behind a Wedding|Whose making, cooking, care, and organizing go uncredited?|Use consented accounts and account for paid and unpaid labor.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Wedding in Context|Which acts are legal, religious, familial, or celebratory?|Define jurisdiction, community, and participants' own terms.
advanced_concepts|Choice and Family Obligation|How do participants negotiate expectations around one practice?|Use varied consented voices without assuming a shared experience.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Customary Origin|Why do two accounts date a wedding practice differently?|Test archival survival, translation, and later retellings.
technology_innovation|A Wedding Goes Online|How did streaming or digital booking alter participation?|Examine consent, access, cost, privacy, and family roles.
people_personalities|A Maker of Ceremony|How did one officiant, artist, or organizer shape a local wedding form?|Use dated evidence and recognize collective authorship.
major_events|Wedding Practice After a Disruption|How did one law, migration, or crisis alter ceremonies?|Separate legal change from social practice with dated sources.
how_it_works|A Ceremony's Sequence|Who decides the order and meaning of one wedding?|Use participant-approved observation and explain variation.
rise_fall|A Custom's Changing Use|What evidence shows more or fewer families choosing it?|Check sampling, geography, class, and generational context.
then_vs_now|One Wedding Practice Across Generations|What changed in roles, costs, and meaning?|Use comparable accounts without calling either form authentic.
future_developments|Choices for Wedding Practice|Which adaptations do participants want?|Compare access, expense, belief, and intergenerational priorities.
myths_vs_facts|A Universal Wedding Rule?|Is a familiar claim actually shared by all members of a community?|Test regional, religious, legal, and family variation.
documentary_stories|One Wedding, Many Roles|How did participants experience a consented event differently?|Protect intimate details and distinguish observation from interpretation.
source_trail|A Wedding Custom in Print|Who first described it for outsiders?|Trace author, language, date, purpose, and omissions.
material_evidence|Objects in a Wedding|What can clothing or gifts reveal about a ceremony?|Check maker, provenance, use, and participant meaning.
chronology_dispute|When Did This Rite Enter Weddings|Which records support rival dates?|Distinguish earlier object use from the named ceremonial form.
ordinary_lives|The Household Cost of Ceremony|How do families and workers bear time and expense?|Use consented accounts, price records, and varied income contexts.
power_and_institutions|Who Authorizes a Marriage|How do law, religious institutions, and families interact?|Name jurisdiction and date; compare formal rules with lived practice.
trade_and_exchange|Wedding Forms Across Diasporas|How do ceremonies adapt after migration?|Trace people, materials, venue, and host-country context.
language_and_labels|Words for Marriage Rites|Which translations obscure participant meanings?|Attribute original terms and contested usages.
maps_and_borders|Wedding Across Jurisdictions|What changes when families marry across legal or cultural borders?|Compare applicable rules and practitioner accounts without legal advice.
conflicting_accounts|Disagreement Within a Family|How do participants value a custom differently?|Present consented perspectives without declaring one representative.
preservation_bias|Which Weddings Enter Archives|Whose ceremonies were recorded and whose were overlooked?|Examine class, gender, religion, and photographer access.
turning_point_test|Did One Trend Change Weddings|What evidence links a new industry or medium to changed practice?|Compare dates, costs, participation, and alternative causes.
legacy_and_memory|Remembering a Family Wedding|How does later memory differ from the event record?|Use consented stories and dated photographs with context.
field_community_ownership|Permission to Film a Rite|Who can authorize documentation and reuse?|Respect couple, participants, custodians, and restricted moments.
field_object_provenance|A Wedding Heirloom's History|Who made, transferred, and interpreted it?|Record ownership and family permissions before publication.
field_living_practice|A Wedding Custom Today|How is a named practice adapted by participants?|Use consented observation and note household variation.
field_conservation_choice|What Should Be Passed On|Which parts of wedding heritage do practitioners prioritize?|Compare their choices with external preservation agendas.
field_cultural_translation|Explaining a Wedding to Outsiders|Which brief explanation avoids flattening meaning?|Check wording with willing participants and disclose limits.
"""

FOLK_TRADITIONS = """history_origins|Earliest Evidence for a Folk Practice|What can a dated source establish about one local practice?|Name community and avoid a single timeless origin.
famous_examples|A Folk Practice in the Spotlight|How does the public version compare with local use?|Ask practitioners about setting, meaning, and variation.
hidden_stories|Unnamed Tradition Bearers|Whose teaching and making sustained the practice?|Use consented accounts and credit collaborative knowledge.
beginner_explainers|What Folk Means Here|Who uses the label and what does it include?|Define form, community, location, and contested terminology.
advanced_concepts|Variation as a Feature|How do versions change across performers and occasions?|Compare attributed examples without ranking authenticity.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Transmission Path|How might a motif have moved between places?|Compare dated records and label gaps honestly.
technology_innovation|Recording a Living Practice|What does digital capture preserve and what does it lose?|Assess gesture, context, consent, ownership, and access.
people_personalities|A Tradition Bearer's Role|How did one named practitioner teach or adapt a form?|Use permission and locate them in a wider community.
major_events|A Break in Transmission|How did a documented disruption affect practice?|Trace migration, schooling, livelihood, or policy changes.
how_it_works|Learning by Doing|How is a folk form taught outside formal classrooms?|Follow a consented apprenticeship, gathering, or household process.
rise_fall|Participation Over Time|What evidence supports a decline or revival claim?|Check venue, generation, survey coverage, and changing labels.
then_vs_now|A Folk Form in Two Periods|What changed in materials, audience, and purpose?|Compare dated examples and practitioner accounts.
future_developments|Community-Led Transmission|Which practical choices could support learning?|Ask practitioners about space, time, resources, and control.
myths_vs_facts|The Unchanged Tradition Claim|Do sources show a single fixed version?|Compare documented variants and current practice respectfully.
documentary_stories|One Teaching Encounter|What happens when a skill or story is shared?|Use consented observation and avoid restricted knowledge.
source_trail|A Collector's Folk Account|What did an early collector record or omit?|Trace methods, language, attribution, and institutional purpose.
material_evidence|A Made Object and Its Use|What can an artifact show about a practice?|Check provenance and compare with living maker knowledge.
chronology_dispute|Dating a Folk Form|Why do archival and oral accounts give different timelines?|Compare what each source dates and its limits.
ordinary_lives|The Practice Between Work and Care|Where does a folk form fit daily schedules?|Use varied local accounts, not festival performance alone.
power_and_institutions|From Local Practice to Official Heritage|Who benefits from recognition and who is excluded?|Compare nomination, funding, access, and practitioner response.
trade_and_exchange|Motifs Across Communities|What evidence shows exchange of forms or materials?|Trace contact without equating resemblance with copying.
language_and_labels|Names Inside and Outside a Community|How do labels shape who gets credit?|Attribute practitioner terms and translation choices.
maps_and_borders|A Practice Across Regions|Where do versions overlap or diverge?|Map attributed examples without assigning exclusive ownership.
conflicting_accounts|Different Uses of One Form|Why do practitioners disagree about meaning?|Present situated, consented accounts without forced consensus.
preservation_bias|The Archive's Selective Ear|Which voices were never recorded?|Examine collector choices, gender, class, language, and access.
turning_point_test|Did a Revival Change Practice|What evidence shows an initiative altered participation?|Compare before-and-after teaching, venues, and alternative causes.
legacy_and_memory|A Folk Form Remembered|How does present memory reshape an older account?|Separate commemoration from evidence of past practice.
field_community_ownership|Who Controls Recordings|What consent governs recording, storage, and reuse?|Ask practitioners about attribution, access, and withdrawal.
field_object_provenance|An Object in a Collection|How did it reach the archive?|Trace maker, collector, transfers, and any dispute.
field_living_practice|Folk Form Outside a Display|How is the practice used now?|Observe with permission in ordinary and public settings.
field_conservation_choice|Keeping Skills Alive|Which safeguard do practitioners actually favor?|Compare training, space, materials, and institutional proposals.
field_cultural_translation|Explaining Local Meaning|Which concepts resist an outsider's short gloss?|Test explanations with willing practitioners and state limits.
"""

